  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The exact area of land is ${(\\frac{7}{9})}^{2}$ hectares.\n\nWriting ${(\\frac{7}{9})}^{2}$ with multiplication signs, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{7}{9})}^{2} & ={{\\frac{7}{9}\\times \\frac{7}{9}}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\times 7}{9\\times 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{7}{9})}^{2}=\\frac{49}{81}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
